K1 MP Eco-Walk
Copyright 2026 Takeyuki-K (https://github.com/Takeyuki-K)

Idea, direction, evaluation criteria and project integration: Takeyuki-K.
The code, model modifications, training pipeline, evaluation tools and documentation were generated and
implemented with Claude (Anthropic), used extensively under the direction, selection, testing and integration
of Takeyuki-K.

The idea is the combination of
  (1) a passive spring-return MP (metatarsophalangeal / toe) joint,
  (2) imitation of human walking data (hip-to-ankle retargeting + IK), and
  (3) learned joint relaxation (variable impedance: policy-selected Kp/Kd)
for energy-efficient humanoid walking.

